      "historicalContext": "A tweakcn homage to Vincent van Gogh's The Starry Night (1889) — the canvas's night blues, swirling sky tones, and points of golden starlight mapped onto interface roles.",
      "colorPalette": "Night sky pigments. Light mode is a daylit version — pale sky `#f5f7fa`, cloud cards `#e3eaf2`, midnight ink `#1a2238`; dark mode enters the painting (`#181a24` ground, `#23243a` cards) with gold `#ffe066` glowing on the blue primary. Night blue `#3a5ba0` leads, starlight gold `#f7c873` seconds and rings, moonlit blue `#6ea3c1` accents, and destructive is a dark plum. Charts sample the canvas — blue, gold, sky, gray, plum.",
